    "turn_text": "Yeah. But I think we got to get to the root cause, which is if we're talking about mental health care, we need to do more with regard to that. And that's one of the things we've been doing in Nebraska, trying to open up lines of communication between educators, mental health professionals, and law enforcement. We need to be more preventative. One of the things we've done in Nebraska is establish our system of care, which is a Again, we're trying to be more preventative with mental health care, especially targeting children, like trying to get to children so that we can keep them in school, not take them in our homes, not do really invasive inpatient type treatment, but get it early on so that they don't have to be pulled out of school and provide, for example, triage lines so that if you can't get to a clinic, we can be able to get some help on a phone line or a Zoom call with a mental health professional. We're investing in just this last legislative session. We had another $5 million to try and encourage people to go into behavioral health and nursing because we've got a huge shortage across the",
