    "turn_idx": 201,
    "turn_text": "Well, the guns are a tool just like anything else. They can be used well or poorly. And that's where I'd get back to. Let's get at the root cause. And I think there's an analogy here with sex trafficking. Sex trafficking is something that happens all over this country. And we need to do more with our law enforcement standpoint, but we also need to be doing more from a participation of the public to be involved looking for the signs of it. And it's one of the things we do in Nebraska is teach, for example, emergency room docs to look for the types of tattoos or teach the general public that You know, be looking out, especially at rest stops and gas stations for someone who doesn't have control of their phone or their ID. Those are signs. And then there's 800 numbers we post on all these places as well. Call in and notify the authorities about this. So to combat sex trafficking, we do need the involvement of the public to be educated. And I think it's the same thing with regard to how do we be more preventative with regard to finding people who are going to be at risk for doing these kinds of things. Again, we have to do the investigation in these, but you look at the parkland, for example, that person had been, cops have been called 45 times and they have to be twice on that person. So there are, I think there are signs out there when somebody's going to do this, We need to",
