    "turn_text": "should have taken your advice. But I do want to ask you about the tenor of our politics, because we're having a good discussion here. But it's so hard to get, there's so much anger and so much outrage. And in our politics, anger and outrage sells in bases of both parties. But I think the president was very good at exploiting that. In our social media, anger and outrage is what keeps people online. It feels like the incentives for cooperation, the incentives for civil discourse have been eroded by a whole range of things. And it worries me as a democracy about how we move forward if I think you are a committed American who cares about this country, cares about his state, even though I disagree with you on some stuff. I hope you think the same of me. But that increasingly is not the norm. We don't have opponents. We have enemies. We have adversaries. How do we diffuse",
