  {
    "episode_id": 90416,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90416.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 296,
    "turn_text": "I agree. And, you know, getting back to Nebraska unicameral. One of the things I mentioned is you've got a filibuster rule that requires 17, you know, you can only take 17 votes to block things. There's 17 Democrats in my legislature. So really to get anything passed, we have to work with the other side to be able to get that passed. When we passed tax relief, we had 41 votes and a lot of Democrats voted for that. Now, I would have loved to pass that bill years ago, getting back to it takes time. But that's the process too. When you're going to war through things, it's going to take time. It's not going to move as fast as maybe people want to do it. But I got to tell you, I tell young people all the time, if somebody old like me tries to tell you about the good old days, they're full of it. These are the good old days. This country has got so much potential in front of us, so many good things are going on right now.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_04",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
